# DineAI Generator Framework Implementation Plan

Implement a decoupled, enterprise-grade LLM generation framework in [generator.py](file:///d:/data/AI_WAITER/dine_ai/llm/generator.py). The framework will manage configurations, request/response DTOs, provider registry, model lifecycle and GPU/CPU memory bounds, caching, validation pipelines, and HuggingFace/Qwen connections. It conforms strictly to SOLID design principles, Clean Architecture, and Strategy/Factory patterns.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The generator framework is divided into distinct structural layers:
> 1. **Data Transfer Layer**: Config blocks (`LLMConfig`, `GenerationConfig`) and DTO payloads (`GenerationRequest`, `GenerationResponse`, `GenerationStatistics`).
> 2. **Provider Registry**: Locator mapping key names to `BaseLLMProvider` instances.
> 3. **Lifecycle Manager**: `ModelManager` isolates memory operations, automatic CPU/CUDA routing, and quantization flags (lazy loading, reuse, unload, reload).
> 4. **Caching & Validation**: `GenerationCache` (LRU prompt hashing with TTL limits) and `ResponseValidator` (checks for leakage, repetitions, length constraints, or broken text).
> 5. **HuggingFace & Qwen Implementations**: `HuggingFaceProvider` wraps tokenizer/device selection. `QwenProvider` integrates actual causal model generation, BitsAndBytes quantization (4-bit/8-bit), FP16, and streaming.
> 6. **Placeholders**: Stubs for OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, Llama, Mistral, and Ollama that raise `NotImplementedError`.

